examples/full/hocon/Proxyfile: auth.jwt.optional: "auth.jwt.optional" is refused by --target haproxy: HAProxy's jwt_verify takes one key file, with no key set, URL, issuer or audience check; verify the token in the service auth.ask names
examples/full/hocon/Proxyfile: routes[1].rpc.retries: "routes[].rpc.retries" is refused by --target haproxy: with retry-on at HAProxy's default, a gRPC call whose connection to the service failed was not sent again, and the wider retry-on that sends it also sends again a request a service may have read; leave retries out of the rpc entry, or render it for envoy
examples/full/hocon/Proxyfile: routes[3].rate_limit.burst: "routes[].rate_limit.burst" above 0 is refused by --target haproxy: HAProxy's rate counts the requests of a period and has no burst; write burst: 0 or leave it out, or render it for envoy
examples/full/hocon/Proxyfile: services.shop.health.grpc: "services.<service name>.health.grpc" is refused by --target haproxy: HAProxy has no gRPC health check: http-check send writes a text body, not the health service's gRPC message; write health.path on the service's http port
examples/full/hocon/Proxyfile: tracing: "tracing" is refused by --target haproxy: the official HAProxy images have no tracing filter (the OpenTelemetry filter is an addon built from source); remove tracing, or render it for envoy
examples/full/hocon/Proxyfile: tracing.path_in_url: "tracing.path_in_url" is refused by --target haproxy: the official HAProxy images have no tracing filter (the OpenTelemetry filter is an addon built from source); remove tracing, or render it for envoy
